Releasing mvm05b.  A few advantages I see of sending out a post each
time I have a new version: I get to write down and think through the
changes I've made; if I don't make any more changes then I don't have
to decide that I'm done; you all get to see the latest version of what
I have; it keeps all the details up to date so I don't forget what I
changed, when, and why; and if you have any comment or advice about
the direction the patch is taking, you can chime in while it's under
development.

But if it's annoying just killfile me, and curse my name when and if
[S] or vanilla contains my code.  ;)

http://www.jcatena.net/nethack/patches.shtml#mvm

DETAILS SPOILER:

Anyway, I add more randomness to the usage of void.  Instead of just
adding void straight up to the to-hit (and subtracting it from the
armor class difference), I pick some random number between 0 and
MonkVoid.  If this number happens to be the max possible value (this
will happen 20% of the time that someone either is using nothing, or
ten things), then I add another modifier in the same range.  If this
also turns out to be the max value, then I print a fun message.

The randomness affects both positive and negative void, so on average
the effects of lowered void will be less noticable.

Void's also now affected by being polymorphed and encumbrance.

